cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SBRUG: Sampling Best Response in Undercutting Games"
authors:
  - family-names: Izquierdo
    given-names: Luis R.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1057-4465"
    affiliation: Universidad de Burgos
  - family-names: Izquierdo
    given-names: Segismundo S.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7113-0633"
    affiliation: Universidad de Valladolid
abstract: >-
  SBRUG is a NetLogo model that compares two ways of revising a strategy in
  undercutting games, such as the traveler's dilemma and the finitely repeated
  prisoner's dilemma: best responding to the strategies of a few randomly
  observed agents (Sampling BR), and best responding to the exact population
  state (Exact BR). Both rules run side by side, on two populations that share
  the revising agents and the experiments.
keywords:
  - sampling best response
  - experimentation
  - unraveling
  - traveler's dilemma
  - repeated prisoner's dilemma
  - evolutionary game theory
  - agent-based model
  - NetLogo
